The database itself does **not** need a `LandingPage` table. This is a **documentation/product specification**, while the landing page is a public frontend experience; the database remains responsible for persistent platform entities such as users, vehicles, journeys, stations, reservations, payments and IoT data. 7

So the clean structure is:

```text
docs/
├── 01-requirements/
│   ├── PRD.md
│   └── LANDING_PAGE.md   ← NEW
├── 02-research/
├── 03-architecture/
├── 04-database/
├── 05-api/
└── ...

This keeps the Landing Page specification aligned with the existing documentation hierarchy instead of mixing UI requirements into the database schema. 